<title>USA: AOL says does not comment on market rumors.</title>
<headline>AOL says does not comment on market rumors.</headline>
<dateline>DULLES, Va. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>America Online Inc reiterated Monday that it does not, as a matter of corporate policy, comment on stock market rumors.</p>
<p>AOL said it was making the statement in response to an article in this morning's Wall Street Journal.</p>
<p>The article said AOL was in talks to buy CompuServe Corp, an affiliate of H&amp;R Block Inc, for up to $1.2 billion in stock.  The Journal said executives familiar with the talks said the companies hope to make a deal as early as this week.</p>
<p>H&amp;R Block owns 80 percent of CompuServe.</p>
